# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# FXA (EXACTNESS of the combination all, WP0): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-audit = the production profile plus QWEN_FAST_CCL_OPTIONS=served,
# QWEN_FAST_CCL_OPTIONS_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_DEVICE_ZEROS=1, QWEN_FAST_DEVICE_ZEROS_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_GATEUP1=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_GATEUP1_AUDIT=1,
# QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_HEAD64=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_HEAD64_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_MM_GRID=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_MM_GRID_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_PERMUTE=1,
# QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_PERMUTE_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_QKV1=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_QKV1_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_REDUCE=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_REDUCE_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_TAIL=1,
# QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_TAIL_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_LAZY_SHARD_W=1, QWEN_FAST_LAZY_SHARD_W_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_MLP_CFG=g3u4d3, QWEN_FAST_MLP_CFG_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX=1,
# QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX_AUDIT=1, QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX_FOLD2=1. Every lever of it runs its audit, which compares the served composition beside the lever on the
# device. READ: c2_smoke_check clean under EVERY lever's rule at once (S1 shard argmax (QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX), MLP streaming config and L1 multiply
# (QWEN_FAST_MLP_CFG), CCL options (QWEN_FAST_CCL_OPTIONS), WP6 F-F1 drafter local reduce (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_REDUCE), WP6 F-F3a drafter SwiGLU and residual kernels
# (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_TAIL), WP6 F-F3c drafter fused gate|up matmul (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_GATEUP1), WP6 R2 drafter matmuls on device-width grids (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_MM_GRID), F-F2
# drafter permutation kernels (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_PERMUTE), F-F3c fused drafter q|k|v projection (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_QKV1), F-F4 one 64-row drafter head
# (QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_HEAD64)): each lever logs its engaged line and an audit line with exact=True, no fell-back line, no 'audit mismatch', no stall, every answer complete.
# ANY mismatch, fallback or missing audit line is NO-GO for the combination: read which lever's rule names it, and ablate with the per-lever pack (references/fusion-jobs).
# every lever that is exact by construction on together, to be timed and audited once before any ablation: the drafter permutations, S1 with the tree fold, the drafter
# reduce, fused q|k|v, tail kernels, fused gate|up weight and device-width matmul grids, the 64-row drafter head, the CCL options at the SERVED (empty) set until the sweep
# names the winner, the MLP streaming config g3u4d3 (card-M sweep: the composed gate, up and down chain 170.4 to 162.1 us per layer, exact), and the two engine-start upload
# levers; NOT the K/V page writer (it needs its card-M proof) and NOT the fused MLP gate|up (its kernels have never compiled on a card). Duration (estimate): 60 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady
